        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Discussion on the Paper by Andrieu, Doucet and Holenstein",
      "bbox": [
        78.57550048828125,
        39.52751922607422,
        316.3913879394531,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generalization of reversible jump MCMC sampling which improves the potentially problematic step of",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        57.378700256347656,
        438.2313232421875,
        65.6905517578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "choosing appropriate between-dimension moves.",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        67.3412857055664,
        226.7900390625,
        75.65313720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In modiﬁed form, this construction is also an ‘exact’ and efﬁcient computational solution to doubly",
      "bbox": [
        51.676300048828125,
        77.30387115478516,
        438.2286376953125,
        85.61572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "intractable problems (see Andrieu et al. (2008)),",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        87.2664566040039,
        223.5962677001953,
        95.57830810546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "fθ.x/= h.θ, x/",
      "bbox": [
        210.5618133544922,
        99.9889907836914,
        265.256103515625,
        115.98799896240234
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "K.θ/ ,",
      "bbox": [
        243.87930297851562,
