        268.8812255859375,
        121.70556640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for unknown K.·/ as well as θ.",
      "bbox": [
        42.70915222167969,
        126.03543853759766,
        157.17422485351562,
        135.1004638671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Miguel A. G. Belmonte (University of Warwick, Coventry) and Omiros Papaspiliopoulos (Universitat",
      "bbox": [
        42.70915222167969,
        146.71372985839844,
        416.7640686035156,
        155.02557373046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pompeu Fabra, Barcelona)",
      "bbox": [
        42.709197998046875,
        156.6763153076172,
        141.9385528564453,
        164.9881591796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We congratulate the authors for a remarkable paper, which addresses a problem of fundamental practical",
      "bbox": [
        42.709197998046875,
        166.63890075683594,
        438.2261047363281,
        174.95074462890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "importance: parameter estimation in state space models by using sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) algo-",
      "bbox": [
        42.709197998046875,
        176.6014862060547,
        438.2270202636719,
        184.913330078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rithms. In Belmonte et al. (2008) we ﬁt duration state space models to high frequency transaction data and",
      "bbox": [
        42.709197998046875,
        186.5640411376953,
        438.2225341796875,
        194.87588500976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we require a computational methodology that can handle efﬁciently time series of length T =O.104–105/.",
      "bbox": [
        42.709197998046875,
        195.41241455078125,
        438.2211608886719,
        204.83908081054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We have experimented with particle Markov chain Monte Carlo (PMCMC) methods and with the smooth",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        206.4897918701172,
        438.2238464355469,
        214.8016357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "particle ﬁlter (SPF) of Pitt (2002). The latter is also based on the use of SMC algorithms to derive maxi-",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        216.4523468017578,
        438.23016357421875,
        224.76419067382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mum likelihood parameter estimates; it is, however, limited to scalar signals. Therefore, in the context of",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        226.41490173339844,
        438.2256164550781,
        234.72674560546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "duration modelling this limitation rules out multifactor or multi-dimensional models, and we believe that",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        236.37745666503906,
        438.23199462890625,
        244.68930053710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PMCMC methods can be very useful in such cases.",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        246.3400115966797,
        236.20359802246094,
        254.65185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this contribution we present a preliminary simulation study which contrasts particle marginal Met-",
      "bbox": [
        51.6751708984375,
        256.30255126953125,
        438.2273864746094,
        264.6144104003906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ropolis–Hastings (PMMH), particle Gibbs (PG) and the SPF methods on simulated data from a linear",
      "bbox": [
        42.708770751953125,
        266.2651062011719,
        438.2220153808594,
        274.57696533203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
